From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcp140: codecvt<char16_t> and codecvt<char32_t> UTF-8 conversions.

Every member of codecvt<char16_t, char, _Mbstatet> and codecvt<char32_t,
char, _Mbstatet> was a FIXME stub returning 0 or NULL. They now convert
between UTF-8 and UTF-16 / UTF-32: in() decodes UTF-8 (1-4 byte
sequences; overlong forms, encoded surrogates, values past U+10FFFF or the
facet's maximum code are errors; an incomplete sequence or no room for both
halves of a surrogate pair is partial), out() encodes, keeping a surrogate
pair together, length() counts the bytes that make at most max characters,
unshift() has nothing to do. The facets keep the maximum code and the
_Codecvt_mode of their constructor (default U+10FFFF, consume_header): a
UTF-8 byte order mark is skipped by in() with consume_header and written
once by out() with generate_header, the state remembering it. The mode
constructor takes the _Locinfo its mangled name has (the spec entries
lacked it).
